      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A good idea would be to make the chatbox not be obstructed by their avatar, avatars or anything within a certain distance, it can be set low enough and not changeable if privacy is a concern. But if one could get that close, then there's no privacy in the first place. (i thought that a user could set how close one has to get to see their chatbox unobstructed, with limits (or \"infinite\" as an option if there's a way to make it so that only the user's own avatar can not obstruct it) and just the ability to turn it off)\n\nThis is still an issue, avatars may obstruct the chatbox anyway by having headwear n other accessories. It's all still an author-made avatar mistake, but it doesn't have to be universally bad when such simple things are not done to fix it and nothing can be really done by anyone else",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
